# What does NOT go to the EAS builder.
#
# ## Read this before adding a line
#
# **`.easignore` REPLACES `.gitignore` for the upload.** Once this file exists,
# EAS stops consulting `.gitignore` entirely — so every exclusion that matters
# has to be stated HERE, even the obvious ones. A `.easignore` that listed only
# "extra" things would make the archive bigger, not smaller, because it would
# silently drop every rule `.gitignore` was providing.
#
# That is what this file is fixing. Without it the archive was ~458 MB: it
# carried `node_modules/` (1.4 GB), `packages/mobile/node_modules/` (1.2 GB) and
# `packages/mobile/android/` (1.5 GB of Gradle output), none of which a builder
# has any use for. With it the archive is the ~1.5 MB of source and manifests
# that the build actually reads.
#
# ## The rule for what stays
#
# EAS runs `npm ci` at the workspace root and then bundles `packages/mobile`.
# So it needs every package MANIFEST (npm resolves the whole workspace graph or
# the install fails), the lockfile, and the SOURCE of the four packages the app
# imports — `schema`, `client`, `authoring` and `github`, which
# `packages/mobile/metro.config.js` resolves to `src` rather than to `dist`.
#
# Nothing below removes any of that. If you are about to exclude something under
# `packages/`, check it against that list first: the failure mode is a build
# that gets all the way to bundling before it says a module cannot be resolved.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Dependencies. EAS installs its own from package-lock.json, which is uploaded.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
node_modules/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The native project.
#
# `packages/mobile/android/` is gitignored and regenerated — EAS runs prebuild
# from `app.config.ts`, which is where the application id, the plugins and
# `blockedPermissions` are actually decided. Uploading a local copy ships
# whatever happened to be on one laptop, and it is the single largest thing in
# the archive.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
packages/mobile/android/
packages/mobile/ios/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Compiled output.
#
# Safe to drop because Metro resolves the shared packages to their SOURCE (see
# the `resolveRequest` block in `packages/mobile/metro.config.js`) — nothing on
# the bundle's path reads `dist/`, and nothing in a managed build would have
# compiled it anyway.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
dist/
coverage/
*.tsbuildinfo

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local state, caches and tooling.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.git/
.expo/
.vscode/
.idea/
*.log

# The workspace root is NOT an Expo project, and a stray config here is how a
# build ends up rooted at it. Kept out of the upload for the same reason
# `.gitignore` keeps it out of the repository.
/app.json
/eas.json

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The announcements repository, cloned here by the Manager.
#
# A separate git repository with its own history, and never part of an app
# build.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/workspace/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Build artefacts and anything holding a secret. Neither belongs in an upload.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.apk
*.aab
*.keystore
*.jks
.env
.env.local
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
